[
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 35748,
    "bookid": 34,
    "chapterId": 372,
    "fileId": 10274,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Differentiated VIN</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Differentiated VIN with condylomatous and basaloid-like features, simulating HPV-associated high-grade squamous intraepithelial lesion. The epithelium displays papillomatous architecture, being notably thickened and showing wide and deep rete ridges. Some areas are of basaloid appearance. The histological findings are indistinguishable from those of HPV-associated high-grade squamous intraepithelial lesion.</p>",
    "source": "Natalia Rakislova",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/34/372/10274.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/34/372/thumb_10274.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 35749,
    "bookid": 34,
    "chapterId": 372,
    "fileId": 10276,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Differentiated VIN</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>p16 staining is negative; this is particularly helpful for differentiated VIN with unusual features, in order to rule out HPV-associated high-grade squamous intraepithelial lesion.</p>",
    "source": "Natalia Rakislova",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/34/372/10276.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/34/372/thumb_10276.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 35750,
    "bookid": 34,
    "chapterId": 372,
    "fileId": 10280,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Differentiated VIN</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Differentiated VIN with unusual features. Abnormal p53 staining characterized by nuclear positivity and overexpression in the basal layer with prominent suprabasal extension.</p>",
    "source": "Natalia Rakislova",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/34/372/10280.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/34/372/thumb_10280.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 35755,
    "bookid": 34,
    "chapterId": 372,
    "fileId": 10285,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Differentiated VIN",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>p53 null staining. There is transition between normal epithelium (wildtype p53 staining) and abnormal, with no p53 staining in the differentiated VIN lesion.</p>",
    "source": "Natalia Rakislova",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/34/372/10285.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/34/372/thumb_10285.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 35757,
    "bookid": 34,
    "chapterId": 372,
    "fileId": 10288,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Differentiated VIN</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Abnormal p53 staining characterized by overexpression in the basal layer with mild suprabasal extension.</p>",
    "source": "Natalia Rakislova",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/34/372/10288.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/34/372/thumb_10288.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 35758,
    "bookid": 34,
    "chapterId": 372,
    "fileId": 10289,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Differentiated VIN</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>The epidermis is thickened and has a parakeratotic surface reaction. The lower layer is composed of abnormal atypical keratinocytes with some mitotic figures.</p>",
    "source": "Natalia Rakislova",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/34/372/10289.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/34/372/thumb_10289.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 35759,
    "bookid": 34,
    "chapterId": 372,
    "fileId": 10290,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Differentiated VIN",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Occasionally, the basal layer can show striking cytological and architectural atypia, but there is still maturation towards the upper layers.",
    "source": "Natalia Rakislova",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/34/372/10290.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/34/372/thumb_10290.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 35792,
    "bookid": 34,
    "chapterId": 372,
    "fileId": 10435,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Differentiated VIN</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>The epidermis shows hyperkeratosis, elongated and anastomosing rete ridges, and prominent intercellular bridges. Abnormal basal atypical keratinocytes are confined to the basal and parabasal layers, in a fully differentiated epithelium.</p>",
    "source": "Natalia Rakislova",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/34/372/10435.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/34/372/thumb_10435.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 35874,
    "bookid": 34,
    "chapterId": 372,
    "fileId": 10599,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Differentiated VIN</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>The epidermis shows hyperkeratosis. The rete ridges are elongated and anastomosing. The basal atypia is notable, with some atypical mitotic figures. Notably, abnormal keratinization is present, with dyskeratosis and a small abortive keratin pearl.</p>",
    "source": "Natalia Rakislova",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/34/372/10599.jpg",
